# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CyberLab .gitignore — keeps secrets, generated files and bulky artifacts out
# of the repository. This is a backstop, NOT a substitute for checking
# `git status` before you commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets and keys (NEVER commit these) ---
*.pem
*.key
*.ppk
*.crt
*.p12
labsuser.pem
cyberlab-key.pem
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.aws/
credentials
aws_credentials
*.env
.env
range/cai/cai.env

# --- Instructor-only material (shared out-of-band, never in the repo) ---
*Answer Key*
*answer-key*
*Answer_Key*
*Instructor*Answer*
TCL_Instructor_Answer_Key*

# --- Generated credentials / rosters (contain student data) ---
rosters/
out/
credentials-*.csv
*-credentials.csv

# --- Release artifacts (attach these to a GitHub Release, don't commit them) ---
*.zip
cyberlab-kit.zip
cyberlab-bootstrap.zip
cyberlab-repo.zip

# --- Logs and runtime output ---
*.log
cyberlab-bootstrap.log

# --- Python build tooling (lab/doc generators) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Docker / local overrides ---
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
